<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTAN GOLD PRICES SEEN UP ON JEWELLERY EXPORT.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN GOLD PRICES SEEN UP ON JEWELLERY EXPORT.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold prices are likely to edge up this week on demand for jewellery exports, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We see a slight rise in the demand of gold for jewellery and its export in the coming months,&quot; dealer Saeed Qureshi of All Pakistan Gem and Jewellers Association said.</p>
<p>Silver prices are likely to remain steady, he said.</p>
<p>Weekly prices:</p>
<p>						     Saturday  August 2</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams 4,410     4,385</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		 6,000     6,000</p>
<p>($1=40.62 rupees)</p>
